# SPA fallback for Netlify-style hosts (Netlify, Cloudflare Pages).
#
# Without this, only "/" exists as a real file: every other route is created by
# React Router in the browser, so a hard refresh, a bookmark or a pasted link to
# /app, /quiz or /results asks the host for a file that was never built and gets
# a 404. The dev server hides this — Vite serves index.html for unknown paths
# itself — so it only ever appears once deployed.
#
# 200, not 301: the browser must keep the original URL so the router can read it.
# Vercel is configured separately in ../vercel.json; this file is inert there.
/*    /index.html   200
